<!--
  RUT_RotSporeKit_SheenWeathers.xml       RotSporeKit - ROT_SHEEN_WEATHER_1 build pass

  rot_kit_spec.md M1 ("The Sheen"), ticket 2: three RUT_ WeatherDefs cloning
  the donor rows RUT_TheRot's baseWeatherCommonalities already used (Rain,
  RainyThunderstorm, FoggyRain) - full field set copied verbatim from the
  live vanilla WeatherDefs (mcp__rimsage__get_def_details, raw/unmerged, this
  pass), edited ONLY on <label>/<description>. This fixes the live ban-3 text
  violation the_rot.md's own header flagged: "a water-rain weather def here
  is a violation... renaming the WeatherDefs themselves is separate, un-owed
  content" - that content lands here.

  rainRate KEPT at 1 on all three (spec: "Keep rainRate behavior so fires
  still douse - the Sheen is wet, it just isn't water"). snowRate/sandRate
  were already absent/0 on all three donors, so nothing to change there.

  String-field sweep for surviving "rain" text (spec's own ❓, closed here):
  - label/description: rewritten below, no "rain" left.
  - weatherThought (SoakingWet): its own label/description read "soaking
    wet" only - no "rain" text, and the Sheen is explicitly wet (spec:
    "it just isn't water"), so this thought stays correct unedited.
  - ambientSounds (Ambient_Rain, Ambient_Wind_Storm, Ambient_Wind_Fog) and
    overlayClasses (WeatherOverlay_Rain, WeatherOverlay_Fog): defName/class
    references only, never surfaced as player-visible text.
  - commonalityRainfallFactor: a numeric curve keyed by map rainfall stat,
    not a string - irrelevant to the sweep.
  No other field on any of the three donors carries free text.

  RUT_SheenExposureLock (GameConditionDefs/, UtinniPatches) is the mechanism
  that actually applies RUT_SheenCoating - these three defs are the reskin
  half only, exactly as ruled ("a RESKIN, not a removal").
-->
<Defs>

  <WeatherDef>
    <defName>RUT_SheenFall</defName>
    <label>Sheen-fall</label>
    <description>The Rot's own reproductive sleet, cloying and glossy, falling in place of rain. It slicks every surface and douses open flame same as any downpour — it is wet, it is simply never water. Anything left uncovered beneath it comes away coated.</description>
    <temperatureRange>0~100</temperatureRange>
    <windSpeedFactor>1.5</windSpeedFactor>
    <accuracyMultiplier>0.8</accuracyMultiplier>
    <favorability>Neutral</favorability>
    <perceivePriority>1</perceivePriority>
    <weatherThought>SoakingWet</weatherThought>
    <rainRate>1</rainRate>
    <moveSpeedMultiplier>0.9</moveSpeedMultiplier>
    <ambientSounds>
      <li>Ambient_Rain</li>
    </ambientSounds>
    <overlayClasses>
      <li>WeatherOverlay_Rain</li>
    </overlayClasses>
    <commonalityRainfallFactor>
      <points>
        <li>(0, 0)</li>
        <li>(1300, 1)</li>
        <li>(4000, 3.0)</li>
      </points>
    </commonalityRainfallFactor>
    <skyColorsDay>
